    "diagnosis": "Chronic lymphocytic leukaemia&nbsp;/ small lymphocytic lymphoma involving the skin",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The predominant cells in chronic lymphocytic leukaemia&nbsp;/ small lymphocytic lymphoma are small lymphocytes with scant cytoplasm and a round nucleus with clumped chromatin. In addition to the monotonous diffuse small cell infiltrate&nbsp;(left), there may be small proliferation centres&nbsp;(right) with clustering of larger cells: prolymphocytes (slightly larger with more dispersed chromatin and small nucleoli) and paraimmunoblasts (large cells with slightly basophilic cytoplasm and round to oval nuclei with dispersed chromatin and central nucleoli).",
    "source": "Antonio Subtil",
    "copyright": "",
